hite king, moved\n\nAnd Black pieces:\n- a7: PBF0 → Black pawn, unmoved\n- c5: PBF1 → Black pawn, moved\n- d5: PBF1 → Black pawn, moved\n- e7: KBF1 → Black king, moved\n- others?\n\nWait, row 2: c2 has BBF1 — black bishop — so yes, black has a bishop on c2.\n\nSo current position:\n- White king on c1, relatively safe.\n- Black king on e7, somewhat exposed.\n- White knight on f7 — a strong outpost, deep in enemy territory.\n- White rook on d2, active.\n- Another white rook on g8 — also deep in enemy territory.\n- Black has pawns on a7, c5, d5 — potential passed pawns?\n- White has central control possibility.\n\nNow, key opportunity: **knight on f7 can jump to d6, attacking the black king on e7**.\n\nNf7-d6: move two down, one left → from f7 to d6? f→e→d (2 left), 7→6→5? No: d6 is one down, two left — that’s not an L-shape.\n\nValid knight moves from f7:\n- ±2 files, ±1 rank or ±1 file, ±2 ranks\n\nSo:\n- f7 +2,+1 = h8\n- f7 +2,-1 = h6\n- f7 -2,+1 = d8\n- f7 -2,-1 = d6 → d6 is f-2, 7-1 → yes, d6\n- f7 +1,+2 = g9 → invalid\n- f7 +1,-2 = g5\n- f7 -1,+2 = e9 → invalid\n- f7 -1,-2 = e5\n\nSo valid: **h8, h6, d8, d6, g5, e5**\n\nAll of these are in the valid move list.\n\nNow, **Nf7-d6**: lands on d6. From d6, knight attacks:\n- e8, f7, f5, e4, c4, b5, b7, c8\n\nDoes it attack e7? d6 to e7 is one right, one up — king move, not knight. So **no**.\n\nBut **Nf7-g5**: g5. From g5, knight attacks:\n- e6, f7, h7, h3, f3, e4, h4, f4 — not e7.\n\n**Nf7-e5**: e5. From e5, knight attacks:\n- d7, f7, g6, g4, f3, d3, c4, c6\n\nNow, **d7**: adjacent to e7 (black king). So knight on e5 attacks d7 — but not e7.\n\nBut **d7 is empty** — but if black king is on e7, then **attacking d7 doesn’t give check**.\n\nHowever, **Nf7-d8**: d8. From d8, knight attacks:\n- b7, c6, e6, f7, f9 (invalid), etc.\n\nNot e7.\n\nWait — is there **any knight move that gives check**?\n\nNone of the knight moves from f7 directly attack e7.\n\nBut what about **discovered attack**?\n\nIf I move the knight, and a 