ng must reach b2.\n- Looking at valid moves:\n  - Queen can go to d2, c3, b3, b2 → Q: b4-b2 is a valid move! This captures the pawn on b2.\n  - After Q:b4-b2, the pawn is gone, no promotion occurs.\n  - Then, with queen and king vs lone king, I can easily deliver checkmate.\n\nOther options like moving the king (e.g., Kb5-c6 or Kb5-a6) are slow and allow ...b2-b1=Q, leading to a likely draw or loss depending on position.\n\nBest move is clearly **Q: b4-b2**, capturing the pawn and preventing promotion.\n\nReason: Capturing the pawn on b2 with the queen immediately prevents Black from promoting and leaves me with a decisive material advantage, leading to an easy checkmate with queen and king vs lone king.\n\nAnswer: Q: b4-b2"}
